  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "Show gates running past 80% of their timeout in orchestrator status",
  "spec": "What: `orchestrator status` reports any gate run that has used more than 80% of its timeout, using gate.running_gates() from T-1392 (orchestrator/gate.py, already merged).\nWhy: a hung gate should be visible before the timeout fires, not after the goal stalls.\nChange cli.py's status branch (cli.py:539-548): the JSON output gains a key \"gates_near_timeout\": gate.running_gates() (list, empty when none). The --plain output prints one line per entry after the codex line: `gate\\t<task_id>\\telapsed=<int>s\\ttimeout=<int>s\\tworktree=<path>`, nothing when the list is empty. A failure reading the registry must not break status (empty list). No other status fields change.\nTests in tests/test_cli.py (unittest.TestCase): patch orchestrator.gate.running_gates (or point its registry at a temp dir) and Pool().status as the existing status tests do; grep tests/test_cli.py first for the current status-test pattern.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_status_lists_gates_near_timeout passes: with one registry entry past 80% of its timeout, status JSON has gates_near_timeout with that task id and --plain prints its gate line",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_status_no_gates_near_timeout passes: with none, JSON has gates_near_timeout [] and --plain prints no gate line",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/cli.py",
    "tests/test_cli.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [
    "T-1392"
  ],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": false,
    "budget_turns": 40,
    "timeout_s": 1800,
    "task_class": "mechanical",
    "route": "straightforward",
    "read_scope": [
      "orchestrator/gate.py"
    ],
    "interface_contract": "consumes gate.running_gates(now=None, threshold=0.8) -> list[{task_id, worktree, pid, started_at, timeout_s, elapsed_s}]"
  },
